John Campbell wrote:
> Davyduck wrote:
>
> > Is there a penalty for chaotics characters killing peaceful monsters?
>
> Yes, there's an alignment penalty. The only characters I've ever
> gotten into alignment trouble with were chaotics who felt the need to
> slaughter a level full of peaceful gremlins.

Over time there are enough hostiles that you can eventually kill
peacefulls with impunity.  The smaller per-hostile alignment bonus
eventually overwhelms the larger per-peacefull alignment penalty
because there are so many more hostiles.

Early on it's necessary to get your alignment up, though.  Perhaps
once you've finished the mines and Sokoban it no longer matters.
Before that trying to avoid killing peacefulls with the occasional
typo leading to a death peacefull will work.



